## 3. Edge Cases Resolved

| Edge Case | How It Is Handled |
|---|---|
| Counter file missing on first boot | `_read_counter()` catches `FileNotFoundError` → returns `0` |
| Counter file corrupted / contains garbage | `ValueError` caught → falls back to `0` |
| Two threads generating IDs simultaneously | Class-level `threading.Lock` prevents race conditions |
| Log directory doesn't exist | `path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` called in logger factory |
| Result is a plain `dict` instead of a dataclass | `_field_getter()` unified getter handles both via `result.get()` / `getattr()` |
| `matched_categories` list is empty | Falls back to `triggered_category` field (backward compatibility) |
| Very long user input | `_truncate()` caps at 120 chars and appends `…` |
| `enable_safe_logs=False` | `log_safe()` returns `None` immediately — nothing written |
| Log files growing unbounded | `RotatingFileHandler` — 10 MB max per file, 5 rotated backups kept |
| Windows file lock during test cleanup | `_close_audit_handlers()` explicitly flushes + closes all handlers before temp dir removal |
| Unknown attack category | `event_type_from_category()` falls back to `"suspicious_activity"` |
| Invalid prompt hardening task name | `get_hardened_prompt("nonexistent")` raises `ValueError` |
| Input containing newlines / carriage returns | `_truncate()` strips `\n` and `\r` before generating the preview |
| Boundary score values (e.g. exactly `0.65`) | `severity_from_score(0.65, True)` correctly returns `CRITICAL` (tested explicitly) |
| Logger handler duplication on re-import | `if not lg.handlers:` guard prevents double-adding handlers |
| `log_safe()` disabled by default | Prevents flooding logs with clean traffic in production |

